'' =============================================================================
'' Single-Step Debugger Test Program D10 — SFR and stack click routing
''
'' Covers Test Plan item:
''   Phase D, D10 — SFR and stack routing into hub mode (Part A §A.3)
''
'' WHY THIS PROGRAM EXISTS: D10 was originally written against
'' test07_stack_ptr.spin2, where three of its four steps are IMPOSSIBLE to
'' perform — that program leaves the interrupt vectors unwritten, sets
'' PTRA=$1000 and PTRB=$2000 (both already hub-range), and leaves only a COG
'' return address on the stack. The tester cannot choose those values at run
'' time, so the steps could not be satisfied. Reported by the 2026-09-07
'' hardware run as "instructions unclear"; the instructions were fine, the
'' program could not produce the states they described.
''
'' This program plants each of the four values D10 needs, at known addresses:
''
''   IJMP1 ($1F4, row 4)  = $00800   an interrupt VECTOR holding a HUB address
''   IRET1 ($1F5, row 5)  = $0F0     an interrupt VECTOR holding a COG address
''   PTRA  ($1F8, row 8)  = $100     a DATA pointer holding a sub-$400 value
''   STK0                 = $00C00   a stack slot holding a HUB-range value
''
'' The PTRA value is the discriminating case for Part A §A.3: it is below $400,
'' yet its row is a data pointer rather than one of the first six interrupt
'' vectors, so it must still route to HUB. A build that tests only the value —
'' the F7 defect — sends it to cog space and fails here.
''
'' PASM-only: cog 0 boots directly into this DAT at $000, so DEBUG_MAIN breaks
'' on the FIRST instruction with nothing in the way.
'' =============================================================================
CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_MAIN = 1

DAT
                org

'' Step through the setup block; every value below is in place by the time
'' execution reaches `parked`.
entry           mov     ijmp1, ##$00800          ' D10 step 1: vector -> HUB address
                mov     iret1, #$0F0             ' D10 step 2: vector -> COG address
                mov     ptra,  #$100             ' D10 step 3: data pointer, value < $400
                mov     ptrb,  ##$2000           '   (a plain hub-range pointer for contrast)

                mov     stkval, ##$00C00
                push    stkval                   ' D10 step 4: STK0 = hub-range value
                                                 '   PUSH's immediate form caps at 511, so the
                                                 '   value is staged in a register first.

'' Park in a tight loop so the panel values stay put while you click them.
'' Nothing below writes PTRA, the vectors, or the stack.
parked          nop
                jmp     #parked

stkval          long    0
